# camofox-extract

Extract clean markdown from any URL using the Camofox anti-detection browser.

## Why?

Regular web scrapers get blocked by Cloudflare, bot detection, and paywalls.
Camofox uses a stealth browser that mimics real user behavior, bypassing these
defenses. This tool wraps the Camofox REST API to make extraction dead simple.

## Install

```bash
pip install camofox-extract
```

## Quick Start

```bash
# Extract content from a URL
camofox-extract https://example.com

# Multiple URLs
camofox-extract https://example.com https://other.com

# JSON output
camofox-extract --json https://example.com

# Raw accessibility tree
camofox-extract --raw https://example.com
```

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `CAMOFOX_URL` | `http://localhost:9377` | Camofox API server URL |
| `CAMOFOX_API_KEY` | (empty) | API key for authentication |

## Python API

```python
from camofox_extract import extract_urls

results = extract_urls(
    ["https://example.com"],
    camofox_url="http://localhost:9377",
)

for result in results:
    print(f"Title: {result['title']}")
    print(f"Content:\n{result['content']}")
```

Or use the client directly:

```python
from camofox_extract import CamofoxClient

with CamofoxClient() as client:
    tab_id = client.create_tab()
    client.navigate(tab_id, "https://example.com")
    client.wait_for_ready(tab_id)
    snapshot = client.snapshot(tab_id)
    print(snapshot)
    client.close_tab(tab_id)
```

## How It Works

1. Connects to a running Camofox browser instance via REST API
2. Opens a browser tab and navigates to the target URL
3. Waits for the page to fully load (network idle)
4. Captures the accessibility tree (lightweight, no screenshot needed)
5. Converts the accessibility tree to clean markdown
6. Returns the extracted content

The accessibility tree contains all visible text, links, headings, and images
without the noise of HTML markup, JavaScript, or styling.

